---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ComplianceCountdown from '../../components/ComplianceCountdown.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="EU Battery Regulation 2023/1542 Guide | EU DPP Provider"
  description="In-depth analysis of Regulation (EU) 2023/1542 requirements, Article 77/78 Battery Passport mandates, 2027 enforcement timeline, and technical checklist."
>
  <div class="py-16 sm:py-24 max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    
    <!-- Hero Header -->
    <div class="text-center max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-16">
      <div class="eyebrow-pill mb-4 mx-auto">Regulatory Knowledge Center</div>
      
      <!-- Balanced Title to prevent awkward wrap -->
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-[1.15] max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        EU Battery Regulation <br class="hidden sm:inline" />
        <span class="text-cyan-600">(EU 2023/1542) Compliance Guide</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-5 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        The European Union's Regulation 2023/1542 establishes the world's most comprehensive regulatory framework for battery design, traceability, carbon accounting, and end-of-life recycling.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex justify-center gap-4">
        <a href="mailto:info@eudppprovider.com" class="neo-btn-primary">
          Request Compliance Assessment →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Countdown Component -->
    <div class="mb-16">
      <ComplianceCountdown />
    </div>

    <!-- Main Content Cards -->
    <div class="space-y-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      
      <!-- Card 1: Scope & Mandatory Categories -->
      <div class="neo-surface p-8 sm:p-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-cyan-100 text-cyan-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm">01</span>
          <span>Scope: Which Batteries Require a Digital Passport?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          According to Article 77, starting <strong>February 18, 2027</strong>, each battery placed on the EU market must have an electronic record (Battery Passport) if it falls into one of these categories:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <span class="text-cyan-600 font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <span><strong>Electric Vehicle (EV) Batteries:</strong> Traction batteries specifically designed for road transport (M, N category vehicles).</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <span class="text-cyan-600 font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <span><strong>Light Means of Transport (LMT) Batteries:</strong> Sealed traction batteries &le; 25 kg powering e-bikes, e-scooters, and light electric mopeds.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <span class="text-cyan-600 font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <span><strong>Industrial Batteries with Capacity &gt; 2 kWh:</strong> Including stationary battery energy storage systems (BESS), telecom backup, and industrial motive power.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Card 2: 4-Tier Information Disclosure Architecture -->
      <div class="neo-surface p-8 sm:p-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-green-100 text-green-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm">02</span>
          <span>Four-Tier Access & Data Disclosure Matrix (Annex XIII)</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The regulation strictly divides more than 70 data points into different access tiers to protect proprietary trade secrets while providing necessary transparency:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs">
          <div class="neo-well p-4">
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm mb-1">👁️ 1. Public Tier (Consumers)</div>
            <p class="text-slate-500">General manufacturer info, battery model, manufacturing date, nominal capacity, chemistry category, carbon footprint performance class, and general recycling take-back instructions.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="neo-well p-4">
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm mb-1">🏛️ 2. Authority Tier (Customs & Market Surveillance)</div>
            <p class="text-slate-500">EU Declaration of Conformity (DoC), Notified Body test reports (UN GTR 20 / ECE R100), full lifecycle carbon audit calculations, and OECD supply chain due diligence audits.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="neo-well p-4">
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm mb-1">♻️ 3. Recycler & Dismantler Tier</div>
            <p class="text-slate-500">Exact weights of critical raw materials (Cobalt, Lithium, Nickel, Lead, Natural Graphite), battery enclosure opening manuals, safety handling instructions, and hazardous component locations.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="neo-well p-4">
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm mb-1">⚙️ 4. Authorized Commercial Actors (OEMs & Refurbishers)</div>
            <p class="text-slate-500">Dynamic State of Health (SOH), internal resistance, state of charge (SOC), cycle history, thermal telemetry, and battery module re-purposing specifications.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Card 3: eIDAS 2.0 & EU DPP Registry Bridge -->
      <div class="neo-surface p-8 sm:p-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm">03</span>
          <span>eIDAS 2.0 Digital Signature & Central Registry Filing</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The EU Commission Central DPP Registry acts as a public lookup directory for unique product identifiers (UPI) and data carrier URLs. Complete battery data remains securely hosted in sovereign enterprise vaults.
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700">
          <div class="p-3.5 bg-white/70 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
            <strong>1. Organization Identity Verification:</strong> Registration via EU Login and issuance of Qualified Electronic Seals (QSeal) or Qualified Signatures (QES) via an EU Qualified Trust Service Provider (QTSP, e.g. DigiCert).
          </div>
          <div class="p-3.5 bg-white/70 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
            <strong>2. PAdES Baseline Digital Sealing:</strong> Tamper-evident PDF/JSON-LD payload signing guaranteeing data integrity before submission.
          </div>
          <div class="p-3.5 bg-white/70 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
            <strong>3. UPI Registration & Official Receipt:</strong> Batch or individual product identifier registration in the EU Central Registry, returning the Registry's own registration receipt, which evidences the filing to authorities and business partners.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Direct Contact Card -->
      <div class="neo-surface p-8 text-center bg-gradient-to-br from-[#F0F4F8] to-cyan-50/40">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">Need Assistance with EU Battery Compliance?</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1 max-w-md mx-auto">
          Our engineering desk provides gap audits, enterprise software licensing, and managed data vault onboarding.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5">
          <a href="mailto:info@eudppprovider.com" class="neo-btn-primary inline-flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>Email: info@eudppprovider.com</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</Layout>
